<p>A federal judge in Washington ordered President Trump’s administration to pause construction of a planned White House ballroom until Congress gives statutory approval, ruling that a president is a steward of the White House rather than its owner. The project, widely reported at about $400 million and described in some coverage as $516 million, moved ahead after the historic East Wing was demolished, and the judge granted a preliminary injunction sought by the National Trust for Historic Preservation. The ruling is a significant legal check on one of the most visible redesign efforts of President Trump’s second term, while still leaving a path for the project to resume if Congress authorizes it. Several reports said the judge delayed enforcement for 14 days to allow for an appeal and avoid disrupting an active construction site, while President Trump signaled that he believed work could continue and the administration was expected to challenge the decision.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/C-qGWptyQkupqYCJa8ofzIW9Lqh9_bsTctylqsjC0K1PeV7v1DdCyIaa4i4p90B-l46TbAzkqmNKYNbXX6SqpPwAjjIM71aE2x-_ACiRXOMgx44_JH5r49vFmTrNP7kxYFNlTHMphuLCQvO1bSqYe2nKucKl2xHb20LzE0x5fltH8LtBKozRsK2zODxuXagr1ELleVfo7s0ztOt4xsDQsibN-lpI9VzE8oVljo0TQUmxz_1F3N8TgqPrnZxsehb-bHFB8vJCT2PrkLoA2w' alt='As seen from the Washington Monument, construction of the White House ballroom continues, Tuesday, March 10, 2026, where the East Wing once stood.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Project scale: The planned ballroom was described as a 90,000-square-foot project on the East Wing site, making it one of the largest physical changes to the White House complex in recent memory.</li><li>Judge appointed: US District Judge Richard Leon, who issued the injunction, was appointed by George W. Bush.</li><li>Preservation lawsuit: The National Trust for Historic Preservation argued that President Trump exceeded his authority by razing a historic part of the White House complex and starting construction without congressional approval.</li><li>Next legal step: The court said Congress could still authorize the ballroom, so the dispute now turns on whether lawmakers formally bless the project or appellate judges narrow the injunction.</li></ul><blockquote>The President of the United States is the steward of the White House for future generations of First Families. He is not, however, the owner! - Judge Richard Leon</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Judge Richard Leon: Leon said the White House cannot be altered this way without Congress and temporarily stayed enforcement for 14 days because the case raises &#x27;novel and weighty issues&#x27; and stopping an active build could create logistical problems. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/judge-orders-halt-on-white-house-ballroom-construction-ruling-leaves-trump-seething/article70809752.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>President Trump: After the ruling, President Trump indicated that he believed construction could continue despite the court order, underscoring the administration’s resistance to the injunction. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/4/1/judge-halts-trump-ballroom-project-trump-says-work-can-go-on'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>National Trust for Historic Preservation: The preservation group sought the injunction, arguing that the East Wing was historic and that demolishing it and starting the ballroom without congressional approval exceeded presidential authority. (<a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/us-politics/article-trump-white-house-ballroom-construction/'>The Globe and Mail</a>)</li><li>Administration legal position: Government lawyers are expected to appeal, reflecting the administration’s view that the president can move ahead with the renovation despite the district court ruling. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/judge-orders-halt-on-white-house-ballroom-construction-ruling-leaves-trump-seething/article70809752.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/court-orders-trump-to-halt-white-house-ballroom-construction/a-76615061'>Court orders Trump to halt White House ballroom construction</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/video-judge-orders-trump-to-pause-construction-of-us400-million-white-house/'>Judge orders Trump to pause construction of US$400-million White House ballroom</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/judge-orders-halt-on-white-house-ballroom-construction-ruling-leaves-trump-seething/article70809752.ece'>Judge orders halt on White House ballroom construction, ruling leaves Trump seething</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/4/1/judge-halts-trump-ballroom-project-trump-says-work-can-go-on'>Judge halts Trump ballroom project; Trump says work can go on</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3348589/judge-halts-trumps-white-house-ballroom-project-unless-congress-approves-it'>Trump fumes as judge halts his White House ballroom project unless Congress approves it</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c7056exw78xo'>Judge temporarily halts construction of Trump&#x27;s White House ballroom</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/news-wrap-judge-orders-halt-to-trumps-white-house-ballroom-construction'>News Wrap: Judge orders halt to Trump&#x27;s White House ballroom construction</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/us-court-blocks-donald-trumps-400-million-white-house-ballroom-project-11293788#publisher=newsstand'>US Court Blocks Trump&#x27;s $400 Million White House Ballroom Project</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/inthenews/comments/1s8yuub/judge_orders_trump_administration_to_halt_white/'>Judge orders Trump administration to halt White House ballroom construction unle